<h1>Belt Conveyors: Types, Materials &amp; Selection Guide</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A belt conveyor uses a continuous loop of flexible material stretched between pulleys to transport products. Unlike <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller conveyors</a> that require flat-bottomed loads, belt conveyors handle products of any shape: bags, pouches, irregular items, small parts, and loose bulk materials. Belt types range from general-purpose flat belts to specialized cleated, modular plastic, and wire mesh designs for specific applications.</p>
<h2 id="subtypes-heading">Explore Belt Conveyor Sub-Types</h2>
<ul class="usa-collection">{beltTypes.map((type) => (
<li class="usa-collection__item"><div class="usa-collection__body"><h3 class="usa-collection__heading"><a class="usa-link" href={type.slug}>{type.name}</a></h3><p class="usa-collection__description">{type.desc}</p>{type.tags && <p class="tags">{type.tags.map((tag: string) => <span class="usa-tag">{tag}</span>)}</p>}</div></li>
